</section>

<section id="s-efficiency" data-code="efficiency">
<div class="section-no">05 — Pareto Efficiency</div>
<h2>Bypassing the Vocabulary Dimension</h2>
<p>In addition to its informational advantages, OPRD-only training is strictly cheaper than output-space variants. Logit-based distillation models require computing and materializing the student next-token probability distribution tensor p<sub>t</sub> ∈ ℝ<sup>B × T × |V|</sup>, invoking a vocabulary-wide log-softmax, and backpropagating through the massive language model head matrix W<sub>head</sub> ∈ ℝ<sup>|V| × d</sup>.</p>

<p>Because OPRD operates entirely before the LM head, it bypasses the vocabulary dimension entirely in the loss path. The memory footprint and computation scale with the hidden dimension d (typically 1536 to 4096) rather than the vocabulary size |V| (typically 150,000). This yields a massive reduction in actor-update peak memory and training wall-clock time.</p>

